### Notes

- **Run it:** put everything in `SortingDemo.java`, then `javac SortingDemo.java && java SortingDemo` (or split each class into its own file — they compile the same way).
- **Why generic `T extends Comparable<T>`:** the same algorithm classes sort `Integer[]` and `String[]` (or `Double[]`, custom objects, etc.). If your instructor expects plain `int[]` only, drop the generics and make `compare(int a, int b)` / `swap(int[], int, int)` the abstract steps instead.
- **Extensibility (OCP):** adding e.g. `InsertionSort` requires zero changes to existing code — just a new subclass implementing the same template contract.
